# The build only needs src/ and the requirements files. Everything else is
# context the daemon copies and then discards.
#
# checkpoints/ alone is 1.2 GB. Without this file every `docker build` ships
# it to the daemon before the first layer runs - on a cross-architecture
# build, once per target. Nothing in the Dockerfile copies it: the deep tier
# fetches its weights from S3 at runtime (see DEPLOYMENT.md, step 3).

# Model weights and scratch audio: large, and fetched at runtime rather than
# baked into the image.
#
# Every directory pattern here is anchored with a leading slash so it matches
# only at the context root. This is deliberate: `audio` unanchored would also
# match src/labs/audio/, which is real source the deep pipeline imports, and
# that is exactly the mistake the .gitignore in this repo used to make. The
# Level-1 ONNX weights under src/labs/screen/weights/ must also survive - the
# screen tier is useless without them, and they are why the *.pt/*.pth/*.ckpt
# patterns below name those extensions rather than a directory.
/checkpoints/
/models/
/audio/
/benchmarks/
/tests/fixtures/audio/
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth

# Local virtualenvs - large, and the wrong architecture for the image anyway.
/.venv*/
/venv/

# Version control and CI.
/.git/
/.github/

# Caches and build artefacts. __pycache__ is intentionally unanchored: it
# appears at every level and none of it belongs in an image.
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
/.pytest_cache/
/.ruff_cache/
/.mypy_cache/
/build/
/dist/
*.egg-info/

# Terraform state and plans: these hold infrastructure detail and, in the
# case of a plan file, variable values. They have no business in an image
# context.
deploy/aws/.terraform/
deploy/aws/*.tfstate
deploy/aws/*.tfstate.*
deploy/aws/*.tfvars
deploy/aws/tfplan*
deploy/aws/backend.hcl

# Secrets and local environment.
*.env
.env*

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
